# Catch linter errors before finishing

After creating or editing any file, run IDE diagnostics (`ReadLints`) on those paths and fix every new error/warning you introduced before reporting done. Do not leave the user to discover lint issues.

## Checklist

1. Edit files as needed.
2. Run diagnostics on every touched path (and related configs if you changed imports/module format).
3. Fix reported issues, then re-check until clean.
4. Only then summarize for the user.

## Project gotchas

- `package.json` has `"type": "module"`. Do not mix `require()` into ESM configs. For Tailwind, use `tailwind.config.cjs` with `require()` (CommonJS-only plugins/types).
- After config renames, update `components.json` / eslint ignores and confirm IDE diagnostics are clean.
- Pest stubs and Inertia page path casing can pass locally and still fail CI; treat both as required.